6. openExpiryBoundary: supplier expiry T0+100d, open at T0. At T0+30d exactly → expired. At T0+30d-1s → ok.
7. idempotentReplay: dispense r1 1.0 → 201; same r1 1.0 → replayed, same id, remaining unchanged; r1 with 2.0 → 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT.
8. recallQuarantinesAndKeepsHistory: two bottles batch B2 (10mL each), one dispensed 6 (remaining 4), other untouched (10). Also a third bottle fully consumed (remaining 0) — dispense 10. recall B2 → quarantined ids = two bottles with remaining>0 (the 4 and the 10), not the 0 one. dispense after recall → BOTTLE_QUARANTINED. detail: dispense history retained (record still there), quarantineReason set.
9. concurrentDispenses: 10 mL, open, dispense 6 (r0). Two threads dispense 3 (rA, rB) with latch. Exactly one success, one 422 INSUFFICIENT_REMAINING. Final remaining 1.0. dispense_record count = 2.
10. detailShowsExpirySourceAndQuarantine — covered in others; maybe merge.

Also test open idempotence: open twice → openedAt unchanged. Add to test 1 or separate.

Concurrency test uses ExecutorService, CountDownLatch, futures with 15s timeout.

Note: service.dispense throws BizException; in threads catch and record. Assert one success one failure with code INSUFFICIENT_REMAINING.

ReagentApiTest: @SpringBootTest + @AutoConfigureMockMvc + @Import(TestClockConfig.class):
- full flow via HTTP: POST /api/bottles → 201; POST open → 200 openedAt; POST dispenses → 201 with remainingAfterMl 4.0; replay → 200 same id; GET /api/bottles/{id} → expirySource OPEN_EXPIRY, remainingMl 4.0, dispenses length 1; POST /api/recalls → quarantinedBottleIds contains id; GET detail → status QUARANTINED, quarantineReason; POST dispense after recall → 422.
- 404 for unknown bottle.
- 400 for invalid body (missing requestId).

JSON path assertions with MockMvc. BigDecimal 4.0 serialized as 4.0 → jsonPath value 4.0. Instants serialized as ISO strings.

One concern: H2 `TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE` in MySQL mode — will find out when tests run. Another: `COMMENT` on columns in MySQL mode — supported.

